<!-- docs/handoff/<actor-id>.md, an agent-to-agent handoff. Terse by design: fragments over sentences,
     pointers over prose. Overwrite on every handoff. Omit any empty section. NO SECRETS, because
     docs/ is tracked; reference locations, never values. Current only while HEAD is BASE_COMMIT. -->
# HANDOFF <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM>

OBJECTIVE: <one line>
APPROVAL: <pending | approved by <name> on <date> | revoked> · SCALE: <scale>
POSITION: sprint <n>/<N> · story <id> "<title>" · status <status> · rounds <n>/3 · retries <n>/2 · verification: <pending|PASS|FAIL|UNKNOWN>

BASE_COMMIT: <git rev-parse HEAD, the last commit of this session>
BRANCH: <current> · INTEGRATION: <branch> · UNCOMMITTED: <none, always, since everything is committed before the handoff>
GATES: test=`<cmd|N/A>` lint=`<cmd|N/A>` build=`<cmd|N/A>`
LAST_GATE_RESULTS: <for example test PASS 2026-07-05 · lint N/A · build PASS>

READ_FIRST: <ordered, minimal; for example docs/stories/S2-1-*.md, docs/plan.md#commands>
SKIP: <looks relevant but is not; spare the next agent the tokens>

DONE_THIS_RUN:
- <story or step: outcome, merge commit or PR>

IN_FLIGHT:
- <story id: exactly where it stopped, which gate or review round, what remains>

OPEN_FINDINGS: <none | reviewer findings not yet fixed, severity + file>

DECISIONS (made this run, not yet in docs):
- <decision, why, and where it belongs: spec, plan, story, or constitution>

GOTCHAS:
- <trap the next agent will hit, and how to avoid it>

BLOCKERS:
- <blocker, and what or who it waits on>

NEXT (ordered):
1. <concrete step: file or command>
2. <...>
